          "text": "⚠️ WARNING: This post contains graphic descriptions of a fatality.\n\nA 13-year-old Chinese exchange student accused of murdering her fellow 14-year-old international student in Newcastle, Australia, arrived in the country with an \"extraordinary\" amount of prescription medication. The two girls were living in the Edgeworth home of host couple Steve Maloney & Tracey Taylor as part of an exchange program.\n\nThe tragedy occurred shortly after 10:30 PM on Monday, August 4, when Tracey heard a commotion, went to investigate, & found the 14-year-old with a stab wound to her torso. Emergency services rushed to the home on Euston Close, but the victim died shortly after arriving at John Hunter Hospital. A kitchen knife, believed to be the weapon, was seized.\n\nThe 13-year-old was formally charged with murder on Tuesday night & appeared in Broadmeadow Children's Court on Wednesday. Magistrate Andrew Eckhold noted the charge was extremely serious & that mental health would be a key factor. He revealed the girl had brought a substantial amount of medication to Australia & that police facts suggest she may have been \"dissociated\" at the time of the alleged killing. The two girls were not known to one another prior to being part of the same exchange. They had arrived from China on July 28 & were due to return home on August 16. The accused's next court appearance is scheduled for October 7, with a Mandarin interpreter.\n\n🙏Please share to spread awareness\nDISCLAIMER: The information shared is based on initial reports, may not be fully verified, and is presented as alleged. Details are subject to change as investigations proceed\n🔔Follow for more recent True Crime Updates\n👁️Source: Daily Mail Australia"
